     "img": "l2_ybor",
     "text": "Claire had a job interview at a dental office downtown at ten o’clock. She left home early, at eight thirty, because she didn’t want to be late. It was her first time taking the bus in Tampa, and she was a little nervous.\n\nAt the bus stop, an older man was reading a newspaper. “Is this the bus to downtown?” Claire asked when a bus arrived. The man looked up and smiled. “This one? Sure,” he said. Claire paid the fare and sat by the window.\n\nOn the bus, she looked at the people around her: a mom with two kids, a young guy with headphones, a nurse in blue scrubs. Everyone looked relaxed. Claire tried to relax too, and she read her notes about the dental office one more time.\n\nAfter twenty minutes, she realized something was wrong. There were no tall buildings and no river. Instead, she saw old brick buildings, colorful murals and chickens walking on the sidewalk. Chickens! She checked the map on her phone. She was in Ybor City, going the wrong way.\n\nClaire got off at the next stop. Her heart was beating fast. It was nine fifteen. She asked a woman at a coffee shop for directions. “Oh, you’re close,” the woman said. “Take the streetcar. It’s free, and it goes right downtown. The stop is just around the corner.”\n\nThe streetcar was old-fashioned and slow, but it was beautiful. Claire watched the city go by and tried to stay calm. She practiced her answers for the interview in her head: “I’m organized, I’m patient, and I love working with people.”\n\nShe arrived at the dental office at nine fifty-five, a little out of breath. The office manager shook her hand. “Did you find us okay?” she asked. Claire laughed. “Eventually! I took the scenic route.” The manager laughed too, and the interview started on a good note.\n\nTwo days later, Claire got a phone call. She got the job. That weekend, she went back to Ybor City on purpose, to see the chickens and to try her first Cuban sandwich.",
